# No watch rule, on purpose, and this file exists to say why rather than to be
# missing.
#
# Upstream and this packaging are the same Git repository. No upstream tarball
# has ever been published: the orig tarball is generated from the tree at build
# time, as debian/README.source describes. So there is no location uscan could
# poll, which is the situation uscan(1) and lintian expect a comments-only watch
# file to document.
#
# This file used to promise a mode=git rule "when upstream starts publishing
# release tags". That promise was wrong twice over. Packaging versions are now
# tagged debian/<version>, per docs/packaging-release.md, and it changed nothing
# here: those are packaging tags on this same tree, not an upstream release
# published anywhere, so a rule against them would have uscan poll this package
# against itself and report it up to date forever. And a git-mode rule could not
# be signature-checked even if one were wanted, because pgpmode=gittag is not
# implemented by the devscripts in resolute (uscan 2.26.7).
#
# What would justify a rule is upstream becoming something other than this
# repository -- a tarball or a tag published elsewhere. Not a tag here.
